    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=### Task\n{{ $('On form submission').first().json.workflow_description }}\n\n### Example Workflow (optional)\n{{ JSON.stringify($('SET').item.json.example_json) }}\n\n### Retrieval Plan\n1. **Vector search**  \n   • Call `kb_search \"<full task + example>\"`.  \n   • Extract ≤ 5 high‑value keywords (APIs, node types, verbs).  \n   • For each keyword call `kb_search \"<keyword>\"`.  \n\n2. **GitHub fallback (only if < 3 snippets so far)**  \n   • Call `github_search \"<keyword> repo:n8n-io/test-workflows path:/workflows\"`  \n     *(up to three calls total).*  \n   • Keep the **five** most relevant snippets overall.  \n\n> Store snippets only in working memory—do **not** output raw tool responses.  \n> Each snippet must carry its `filename` so it can be cited later.\n\n### Build the Workflow\n1. Use the snippets to pick sensible defaults (trigger, auth, error handling, …).  \n2. If you include a **Tools Agent** (`@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent`) you **must**:  \n   • Wire **OpenAI Chat Model → ai_languageModel → Agent**  \n   • If you add **wfs Postgres PGVector**, wire **ai_tool → Agent**  \n3. Insert one Sticky Note at the top citing every filename you relied on.  \n4. Put all runtime options inside `parameters`; wrap code in `try/catch`.\n\n### Final Output  \nReturn **one** JSON object wrapped in a single ```json``` block, containing **only**:\n\n{\n  \"name\": \"<title>\",\n  \"active\": false,\n  \"nodes\": [ … ],\n  \"connections\": { … }\n}\n\nNo arrays, no extra keys, no markdown outside the code block.  \nIf the Tools Agent is present but mis‑wired, reply exactly  \n`{ \"error\": \"Mis‑wired Tools Agent\" }`.\n",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=ROLE\nYou are a senior n8n Workflow Builder.\n\nTOOLS\n• kb_search  – vector KB snippets (fast, curated).  \n• github_search – GitHub code search; use queries like  \n  \"repo:n8n-io/test-workflows path:/workflows <keyword>\".\n\nPOLICY\n• Follow the Retrieval Plan above: vector first, GitHub only if needed.  \n• Never emit intermediate tool results—only the final workflow JSON.  \n• If you create a Tools Agent, it must be wired as specified; otherwise\n  omit it entirely.  \n• On validation failure output the exact error JSON requested by the user\n  message (no markdown, no text).\n"
        }
      },
